<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's Centralcer H1 profit after loss.</title>
<headline>Portugal's Centralcer H1 profit after loss.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan 1 to June 30:</p>
<p>(billion escudos, unless stated)</p>
<p>Net 0.220 vs 0.313 loss</p>
<p>Cons net  1.173 vs 0.305 loss</p>
<p>Operating result 1.349 vs 1.229</p>
<p>Financial result 1.324 loss vs 1.338</p>
<p>Turnover 20.237 vs 19.562</p>
<p>Extraordinary gains 1.594 vs 0.117</p>
<p>Note - Central de Cervejas is Portugal's second biggest brewer.</p>
<p>A statement from the company said: &quot;The restructuring of the financial liabilities, one of the objectives for the current year, concluded satisfactorily with the issue of nine billion escudos worth of bonds with a term of five years. This operation will be reflected positively in the current results, mainly from the second half of the year.&quot; It added: &quot;The strong growth in extraordinary results is due to the profit from the sale of real estate which does not affect activity.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom 351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
